.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/25/code.py:384:def _main_no_split(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/20/code.py:58:#    examples, a human can see that isolated black dots in blue are not highlighted\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/20/code.py:59:#    while black pixels hanging from large regions by a corner are highlighted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/20/code.py:184:    - The highlighted cells are not \"all small black defects\" anymore; they are only the dangling endpoints of large 8-connected black structures, including diagonal corner attachments that would not qualify under the original 4-connected reading.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/2/code.py:169:    Key insight: The same grey color can either be highlighted or erased, so enclosure by the surrounding region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/32/code.py:333:def _build_base(split_r: int, split_c: int, decor_r: int, decor_c: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:207:    is a defect to highlight, while grey inside black is noise to erase.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/21/code.py:50:#   Arrows are larger than the old T markers, so the generator slightly favors roomier boards and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/25/code.py:27:#    index 0..k-1 is mapped to a fixed light-to-dark rainbow palette, so color is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/26/code.py:75:#       light blue always means \"old location kept as context\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/34/code.py:83:   - At the same time, thin black edge protrusions are no longer highlighted, distinguishing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/34/code.py:256:    Highlight only the deep black cores of blue-embedded defects, then halo them in orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f