rget colors so highlighting is visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/23/code.py:41:    highlight rule depends on legend-color membership rather than on a single special color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/23/code.py:65:    highlights inside unmatched rectangles are visually different and both tied to the same legend frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/23/code.py:85:    kept component triggers the partial highlight branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/23/code.py:87:    is forced to contain highlightable target-color pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/23/code.py:128:    Recolor palette-complete components and highlight legend-colored pixels in the rest.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/23/code.py:140:    Key insight: The legend now controls both which components are \"complete\" and which color marks them, so full matches become solid border-color blocks while partial matches reveal their target-color locations by in-place highlighting.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/23/code.py:266:def _highlight_patch(patch: np.ndarray, targets: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/23/code.py:303:        transformed = _recolor_patch(patch, BORDER) if matched else _highlight_patch(patch, targets)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/5/code.py:90:def _split_frames(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[np.ndarray], int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/13/code.py:138:def _split_frames(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[np.ndarray], int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/38007db0/5/code.py:37:#    input rows show one slightly denser cell, while outputs keep only those extra pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/23/code.py:129:def _split_frames(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[np.ndarray], int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b0280bc/8/code.py:58:    Key insight: The output is no longer a flat \"path highlight\"; it is a fully typed path\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/38007db0/13/code.py:60:  mirror-only sprite pixels, so the output is a sparse but non-empty highlight.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/38007db0/22/code.py:69:#    per column, plus outputs that are sparse highlights rather than full copied\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/38007db0/6/code.py:51:#    but compact, so they read as highlights rather than noise. No object overlap or extra marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/8/code.py:64:#     must be split into interior and ray subsets before writing colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/38007db0/12/code.py:42:#    output becomes a sparse highlight of those removed pixels. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/38007db0/12/code.py:72:#    single variant (copy odd-minus-base additions) because here the highlighted\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/25/code.py:644:def _generate_irregular_split_line_constrained(width: int, base_y: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/25/code.py:657:def _extract_pieces_from_splits_constrained(width: int, split_lines: list[np.ndarray], length: int, max_height: int) -> list[np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/25/code.py:682:def _generate_split_pieces(width: int, length: int, num_pieces: int) -> list[np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/25/code.py:717:    light_choices = order[-3:]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/25/code.py:719:    light_pool = [c for c in light_choices if int(c) != dark]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/25/code.py:720:    light = int(np.random.choice(light_pool))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/25/code.py:721:    return [dark, light]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/8/code.py:21:#   2. read its direction: dark->light means \"this chain uses source pieces from darker to brighter\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/8/code.py:22:#      light->dark means the reverse;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/8/code.py:28:#   a top-side legend [maroon, yellow] means a 2-piece chain with source order dark->light. If the two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/8/code.py:59:# - The ordering cue is human-visible: legend runs are explicitly dark->light or light->dark, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/8/code.py:104:ORDER_MARKERS = [9, 5, 4]  # dark -> mid -> light\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/28/code.py:48:#    - The generator separates cleanup markers from dent patches and lightly spaces cleanup markers from one another, which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/20/code.py:32:   - the control pixel's own row/column is promoted to a full yellow splitter ray\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/20/code.py:55:   - \"one source span drives one global pass\": false once a splitter ray cuts the grid first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/20/code.py:63:   - blobs do not occupy the splitter line, so the measuring bar remains the first ray hit and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/20/code.py:262:def _unsplit_output(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int, src: dict[str, object]) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/41/code.py:43:#     count is reduced slightly and pair-dents are disabled to keep samples readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/17/code.py:543:def _generate_irregular_split_line_constrained(width: int, base_y: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/17/code.py:560:def _extract_pieces_from_splits_constrained(width: int, split_lines: list[np.ndarray], length: int, max_height: int) -> list[np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/17/code.py:592:def _generate_split_pieces(width: int, length: int, num_pieces: int) -> list[np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/9/code.py:59:#       the border itself highlights which pixels are special sources, and the quadrant determines which corner of the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/18/code.py:44:#      a top touch that looks \"slightly inward\" on the thick border can map farther inward inside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/37/code.py:59:#     stay in bounds. Inner/outer footprints within one family may overlap slightly,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/28/code.py:35:#   lighter gradient colors. If one incorrectly used the legend-touch point as the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/22/code.py:547:def _generate_irregular_split_line_constrained(width: int, base_y: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/22/code.py:563:def _extract_pieces_from_splits_constrained(width: int, split_lines: list[np.ndarray], length: int, max_height: int) -> list[np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/22/code.py:593:def _generate_split_pieces(width: int, length: int, num_pieces: int) -> list[np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/9/code.py:51:#   raised slightly so a full blocker stripe and a visibly truncated L can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/10/code.py:54:# - The frame size stays near the base ranges but uses slightly larger minimums so a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/39/code.py:39:     gradients, so \"lighter outward border\" is learnable from 2-4 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/39/code.py:84:     layers become lighter according to a small repeated palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/39/code.py:266:      layer to the center uses the target color, the next layer uses a lighter\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/39/code.py:267:      intermediate color, and any farther layer uses the lightest outer color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/13/code.py:70:    Launch two opposing periodic rays on each active line; companions recolor each ray mid-flight.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/16/code.py:454:def _solve_split_mode(pieces: list[dict], legend_idx: int, legend_map: np.ndarray) -> list[np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/16/code.py:941:def _split_mode_instance(palette_shape: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[list[np.ndarray], np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/28/code.py:316:    row_split = np.array([ROW_BASE + bank[\"row_offsets\"][i % len(bank[\"row_offsets\"])] for i in range(w)], dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/28/code.py:317:    col1_split = np.array([COL1_BASE + bank[\"col1_offsets\"][i % len(bank[\"col1_offsets\"])] for i in range(h)], dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/28/code.py:318:    col2_split = np.array([COL2_BASE + bank[\"col2_offsets\"][i % len(bank[\"col2_offsets\"])] for i in range(h)], dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/24/code.py:29:#     - The input count range is expanded slightly beyond the original 1-3 family\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/10/code.py:336:# Sprite geometry: slightly smaller than the source task to improve placement success.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:399:    Create a one-hole shell with slight irregularity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/30/code.py:23:  D8 code is still useful because it highlights which original assumptions about control-sequence direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/41/code.py:24:#         nearest the anchor takes the darkest ramp color and the fourth piece takes a lighter ramp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/41/code.py:34:#      is always mapped to the darkest ramp endpoint and the last piece to the lightest endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/41/code.py:63:#    - The chain topology makes the gradient easy to read: darker near the anchor, lighter farther\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/41/code.py:276:    - Record the order in which sprites attach to the growing assembly. After assembly, recolor each moved sprite according to that step order using a fixed dark-to-light ramp, while keeping red connectors red and the anchor yellow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/24/code.py:29:#    - Small boards use slightly fewer sprites and fewer special events so the same interaction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/2/code.py:61:#         solver therefore uses exact morphology matching and only a light density-based score\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/1/code.py:56:#      in-bounds, unambiguous, and free of mid-flight sprite crossings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b99e7126/45/code.py:326:def _split_mask_into_fragments(mask: np.ndarray, fragment_count: int) -> list[np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/11/code.py:14:#       - The whole ray is now visible, and the trail color encodes flight phase rather than\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/7/code.py:15:#      2) the whole 5-step flight becomes visible; steps 1..4 are painted maroon 9,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b99e7126/8/code.py:97:    - The odd cell is still a miniature blueprint for a larger 3x3 placement, but the enlarged placement is no longer a plain completion. It behaves like a toggle mask whose \"off\" state is a carved background hole, so the given clues disappear and the missing active positions light up.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/38/code.py:56:   - To make the fused rule human-visible, the generator emits a slightly richer frame family:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b99e7126/33/code.py:168:    - A 29x29 grid is split into a 7x7 array of 3x3 cell interiors by single-color divider lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:40:#      the path length is no longer fixed and the route can jump non-locally mid-flight.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/4/code.py:33:#    - The generator always includes at least one genuine mid-flight intersection, not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:11:#      along the ray. D6/0 makes the whole flight visible instead of only the final\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/19/code.py:12:# - I model the gravity arc as a 5-cell discrete flight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/19/code.py:21:# - Output paints every in-flight background cell on that fused path in maroon 9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/19/code.py:68:#   9 = visible flight cells, lone bg landing, or hit sprite recolor;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/24/code.py:348:    # Bias slightly toward deeper branches so 1/2/3-marker cases all appear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:18:#    - One highlighted color is upgraded further and receives both opposite-edge pairs,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:57:#    - The highlighted contest color provides repeated evidence inside one sample instead of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:66:#      junction-side turn, so the output highlights the intended route rather than cluttering\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/26/code.py:24:#    - Original 142ca369 paints every free-flight ray cell, recolors the bounce\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/26/code.py:27:#      wording literally: the ray is invisible during free flight and only the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/26/code.py:33:#        input:  blue arrow ... invisible diagonal flight ... orange wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/26/code.py:39:#          - all free-flight diagonal cells stay background,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/26/code.py:42:#          - outgoing free-flight cells also stay background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/26/code.py:360:    hidden_flight_cells = int(np.sum((g == bg) & (combo == bg) & (continuous_surround != bg)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/26/code.py:364:        \"hidden_flight_cells\": hidden_flight_cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/26/code.py:542:    if metrics[\"hidden_flight_cells\"] <= 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:396:        \"outputs_differ_from_split_only\": not np.array_equal(combo_out, split_only_out),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/35/code.py:215:def _solve(grid: np.ndarray, *, split_by_band: bool, recolor: bool) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/7/code.py:45:#      far it travels, and the path it actually used is highlighted by the ordered trail 4->8->6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/12/code.py:483:# Slightly favor 2-pair scenes so the opposite-frame D8/2 signal is visible in a small training set,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/21/code.py:437:    # bias the proposal slightly toward 4 to keep accepted samples balanced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/30/code.py:36:#      - all free-flight cells away from the bounce remain background;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:42:#       language is clearly \"gravity cave\", not a slightly modified winding corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/29/code.py:100:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/43/code.py:344:def _split_open_area(frame_mask: np