snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/15/code.py:28:#    sprite exists in the top region, it must not suppress a light shared-hole sprite in the bottom region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/15/code.py:37:#    one region dark beats light only when both compete for the same local hole-count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/15/code.py:44:#    colors across regions, providing a concrete cue for local matching. The light/dark distinction uses only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/15/code.py:50:#    and light grey; the generator enforces that palette restriction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/15/code.py:200:      drawn in light grey and dark grey.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/15/code.py:207:    - A matching light sprite recolors only if the same region does not also contain any dark sprite with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/15/code.py:609:    - region A has a dark-vs-light conflict on the shared hole-count,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/15/code.py:610:    - region B has a light-only winner for that same shared hole-count,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:11:#      - light blue (8) = effectively width 1.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:18:#      - Fused task on the same wide geometry but with the downstream suffix recolored light blue:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:19:#        the 2×2 square stops at the last dark-blue placement before the light-blue suffix.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:25:#    - Only one extra input degree of freedom is added: corridor color state {dark blue, light blue}.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:27:#    - The clues repeat within each sample as long light-blue suffixes, so the rule is observable without\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:41:#      suffix to light blue; recoloring cannot create overlaps or out-of-bounds placements.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:48:#      - large mover + light-blue suffix => stops before the suffix,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:49:#      - 1×1 mover + light-blue suffix => still reaches and ends red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:52:#    - The scene still has only five meaningful colors: green, dark blue, light blue, black, red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:59:#    - For intended stuck samples with n>=2, the generator explicitly verifies that if light blue were\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/3/code.py:106:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/11/code.py:94:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray], list[int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/40/code.py:187:      the output then highlights only the hole-adjacent inner border rather than repainting the entire object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/40/code.py:218:# Slightly larger workspace preserves the same legend/sprite logic while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/7/code.py:58:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/17/code.py:75:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/15/code.py:97:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:83:#    - In overflow cases the outside ring lights up immediately around the square,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/20/code.py:108:def _split_colored_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray], list[int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/s