:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D11/2/code.py:84:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D12/1/code.py:115:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D12/2/code.py:83:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D15/0/code.py:114:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D14/1/code.py:60:#   - The separator cleanly splits the panes, sprites live only on the left, and rays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D4/1/code.py:77:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D15/2/code.py:88:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D4/2/code.py:69:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D10/1/code.py:249:    Trace a solid square through a winding river and highlight the chokepoint when the fit fails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D10/3/code.py:12:#     - 原题里，一个发射器即使起初离分隔线较远，只要它右移后洞会落到 sep-2，就会在对应行发射红线。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D10/3/code.py:13:#     - 本变体里，同一个发射器如果起初左移了 1-3 格，那么在发射判定发生时它的洞还没到 sep-2，因此不会发射；之后再平移也不会补发射。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D10/3/code.py:14:#     - 只有输入中本来就 flush 的发射器会留下红线，而其他发射器只会在左侧移动，不会在右侧留下痕迹。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D10/3/code.py:16:#     - 保持原题的精灵类型、带状排布、>=60% 发射器比例和窄右半区，避免引入新的识别任务。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D10/3/code.py:17:#     - 为了让 D10 差异稳定可见，生成器强制“至少一个发射器 flush、至少一个发射器 non-flush”，这样同一题里同时出现会发射和不会发射的封闭洞。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D10/3/code.py:27:#     - 人类能直接看到：有些“洞形发射器”输入时已经贴着分隔线，所以输出有红线；另一些形状相似但离分隔线更左，输出只移动不发光。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D10/3/code.py:31:#     - band 之间至少隔一行背景，避免多个候选发射器在视觉上粘连。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7666fa5d/D8/1/code.py:305:def _build_input_grid(line: int, segs: list[tuple[int, int, int]], split_idx: int, split_plan: tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int], list[int]]) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D13/0/code.py:125:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D13/2/code.py:92:def _split_canvas(g: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/0/code.py:49:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:59:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D9/1/code.py:25:#     - The connector is now a full 2-row block instead of a single highlighted row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D8/0/code.py:73:#       origin-highlight color, so there is no arbitrary color mapping to infer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D2/0/code.py:71:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D8/2/code.py:47:#     slightly toward chain lengths 2-3; otherwise too many samples would look\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/0/code.py:60:#       repeated lattice with one highlighted translated block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/0/code.py:298:def _split_mask_into_fragments(mask: np.ndarray, fragment_count: int) -> list[np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D2/3/code.py:67:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D2/2/code.py:58:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D5/0/code.py:33:#   - 如果只允许四个角做源，规则会过于接近“角落发射器”，抽象性不够，也会减少布局自由度。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D8/2/code.py:66:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:305:def _solve_split_views(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D1/0/code.py:73:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D1/1/code.py:58:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D1/2/code.py:52:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D3/0/code.py:84:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D6/0/code.py:83:    Key insight: Green bars still encode direction and thickness, but D6 changes each ray from \"first-hit only\" into a full line scan that can light multiple blobs before reaching the boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D3/1/code.py:58:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D7/1/code.py:67:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D3/3/code.py:65:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D7/2/code.py:71:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D3/3/code.py:33:#     unpainted_free_flight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D3/3/code.py:51:#       the short outgoing marker is visible and still followed by blank flight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D12/0/code.py:77:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D14/0/code.py:392:def _split_connected_canonical(pts: np.ndarray, W: int, max_area: int) -> list[list[tuple[int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D12/1/code.py:55:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/0/code.py:411:def _split_output_components(out: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, list[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...]]]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/0/code.py:56:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D15/1/code.py:43:#       the same route is present, but the \"active distance boundary\" is highlighted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D15/1/code.py:177:    Extend the green route across the grid and highlight the exact keep-out boundary where the detour becomes tight.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D15/1/code.py:188:    Key insight: Blue cells do double duty: they still set how far the path must stay away, and now they also determine which parts of the final path are highlighted as exact-boundary contact.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/2/code.py:117:    Add red outlines around objects, and highlight the components that do not enclose holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/3/code.py:74:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/2/code.py:14:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/2/code.py:267:    Reassemble scattered fragments into a dense left-right symmetric rectangle, then highlight its joins.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D4/3/code.py:252:    Key insight: The path geometry is unchanged; only its rendering changes. Blue still tells you how far the hidden route must stay away, while green now highlights the route's turning points instead of tracing every step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D6/1/code.py:83:def _split_sections(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[str, list[np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D4/1/code.py:145:    Recover the shared 20x20 motif, then highlight where the observed crop came from.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D16/0/code.py:121:def _split_frames(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[np.ndarray], int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:14:#      variant: if a dark 2-hole sprite and a light 2-hole sprite both appear,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:15:#      only the dark sprite becomes red and the light sprite is erased to BG.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:16:#      If only light 2-hole sprites appear, they become red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:21:#      same-hole light-vs-dark conflict and at least one light-only winning hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:31:#      light sprites even when dark sprites with the same hole-count should take\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:41:#      and a fallback case (same legend system, only light shade available).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:53:#      light sprites of the same hole-count should lose; generator always creates\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:143:    - Workspace sprites come in two source shades: light grey and dark grey.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:149:      that hole count are recolored; light-grey sprites with the same hole count are erased.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:150:    - If a legend hole count has no dark-grey sprite, matching light-grey sprites are recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:158:    light_grey = 5\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:161:    legend = _legend_mapping(g, bg, (light_grey, dark_grey))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:166:    for shade in (light_grey, dark_grey):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:602:    - at least one legend hole-count where dark wins over light,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:603:    - at least one different legend hole-count where light wins because no dark exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:611:    light_only_hole = random.choice(other_holes)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:613:    winner_shade: dict[int, int] = {priority_hole: DARK_GREY, light_only_hole: LIGHT_GREY}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D10/2/code.py:40:#    - Sprite counts are trimmed slightly because the legend panel is taller / wider than before.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a25697e4/_variant_lib.py:479:def _scene_split() -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D4/0/code.py:153:    - Matching is still decided purely by topology, but the output highlights each matched sprite's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/0/code.py:39:#    - The number of sprites is reduced slightly and a queue band is reserved so\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
